okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Direct gateway data path: capability guard that keeps launches whose channel wakes need router body injection on the router (plain Codex TUI mandatory), keeps codex-remote/app-server direct, and checks other plain modes."
reported: >
  Parent instruction 2026-10-16 (user approved implementation + verification; no commit/push/install/live changes):
  plain Codex TUI must fall back to router mode when configured direct, because the Windows short wake marker relies on
  router HTTP body injection. Provider-neutral/capability guard, fallback status reason, test the actual plain launch and
  that restart retains the router, keep codex-remote/app-server direct, check plain modes on other platforms and fail
  closed where appropriate. Existing dirty changes kept.
context:
  concurrent_editor: "Another agent (direct-gateway-impl) was still editing launch_data_path.py, runtime_launch.py, channel_pending_injection.py, codex_desktop_injection.py and tests until 16:28 local (journal revision_2026_10_16_seam_review in ../cielairouter-direct-path.okf). Edits here started after 6+ minutes without file changes and were re-checked before editing. Its runtime-name branch (if runtime == 'codex') was replaced; its whole-message delivery flag (CIEL_RUNTIME_DIRECT_GATEWAY_ACTIVE) was kept unchanged."
code_paths_inspected:
  - "runtime_launch.run_codex: subprocess_call_with_channel_wake_proxy(wake_for_llm_delivery=channel_delivery_mode(cfg)=='llm', channel_wake_display_body=os.name!='nt'). Codex has no messaging socket, so default session_socket requests fall back to router transport (channel_pending_injection.py fallback=router)."
  - "channel_message_prompt.format_llm_delivery_wake_prompt: '[ciel-wake] pending_ids=N' only; format_visible_llm_delivery_wake_prompt adds the body (non-Windows Codex) while keeping router replacement semantics."
  - "channel_wake_context.body_with_pending_messages -> channel_llm_context.inject_pending_channel_context: the router strips the wake turn and appends format_llm_batch_prompt(pending) to the model request; FIFO guard raises ChannelLlmInjectionDeferred behind earlier TTY-owned messages."
  - "runtime_launch.run_claude: proxy wake_for_llm_delivery=llm_channel_delivery, no channel_wake_display_body (False) -> router-transport wakes are bare markers on every platform; whole messages only via the messaging socket (prepared_socket_path returns '' when claude_code.session_socket_input is false)."
  - "codex_app_server_session: remote TUI runs with inject_channel_messages=False; CodexAppServerChannelInjector submits whole messages as app-server turns (RPC)."
  - "docs/journal/2026/10/03/diagnostics/channel/codex-typed-prompt-chars-dropped.okf: typed bodies lost U+2026/U+2014/U+23F0 in Windows Codex; the dropping layer was not determined."
design:
  capability: "launch_data_path.ChannelDelivery(terminal_wake: bool, whole_message: str); router_reason() returns CHANNEL_MARKER_REASON when terminal_wake and no whole_message transport. resolve(..., channel=) and LaunchDataPathResolver.__call__(..., channel=) check it after the provider capability check and before policy.launch_gateway (no discovery/probe), record it, log one WARN line and print the fallback line. No runtime-name or provider-name branch."
  reason: "channel wakes are typed [ciel-wake] markers whose bodies only router model HTTP injects (no whole-message transport)  (113 chars; records keep 160)"
  declarations:
    plain_codex: "ChannelDelivery(terminal_wake=channel_delivery_mode(cfg)=='llm') -> router on every platform; restart: launched_direct is False so no reselection, and _reselect_codex_data_path also receives the same channel."
    claude: "ChannelDelivery(terminal_wake=stdin_channel_proxy and llm_channel_delivery, whole_message='session_socket' if a socket target exists) -> direct allowed with the messaging socket (or without a wake proxy); router when session-socket input is off. Reselection on restart re-evaluates with the current socket target."
    app_server_and_codex_remote: "ChannelDelivery(whole_message='app_server') at launch and relaunch -> direct still allowed."
  other_platforms: "Non-Windows plain Codex types the body after the marker (display_body), so content would arrive without the router, but that turn is designed around router replacement and was not verified without the router (no non-Windows host here); it stays on the router (fail closed). Claude Code: the marker-only path exists on every platform, so the socket-off case falls back everywhere."
files_changed:
  - "ciel_runtime_support/launch_data_path.py: module docstring, CHANNEL_MARKER_REASON, ChannelDelivery, resolve(channel=), resolver channel check replacing the runtime == 'codex' branch, status_lines text, __all__."
  - "ciel_runtime_support/runtime_launch.py: run_claude claude_channel_delivery() used at launch and restart reselection; run_codex codex_channel at launch and restart; _reselect_codex_data_path(channel=); run_codex_app_server app_server_channel at launch and relaunch."
  - "tests/test_launch_data_path.py: Claude/Codex harness options (socket, stdin_proxy, delivery_mode, parent bypass flag and wake options capture) and 7 new/strengthened tests."
  - "docs/Configuration.md, docs/Module-Map.md, CHANGELOG.md (Unreleased)."
verification:
  environment: "Windows 11 26200, Python 3.11.6, ruff 0.14.11; all inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* names removed (env -u) for every test and E2E run; tests through scripts/run_test_group.isolate_runtime_state (evidence/focused.py)."
  unit_new_file: "evidence/launch-data-path-tests.txt: tests/test_launch_data_path.py 41 tests OK (verbose). New or strengthened: resolver marker-only channel keeps router before selection (0 launch_gateway calls, WARN line, record + status line carry the reason, reason <= 160 chars); whole-message transport, no terminal wake or no channel permit selection; channel adds nothing to router mode or to other providers; plain Codex run_codex launch + restart both on the router provider block (ROUTER_BASE/v1, router alias -m, CIEL_RUNTIME_CODEX_API_KEY, no gateway key or ciel-runtime-gateway id, parent direct-delivery flag unset, wake_for_llm_delivery True) with 0 selections; capability not runtime name (delivery_mode tty -> plain Codex selects gw1, restart gw2); Claude socket off -> router at launch and restart, 0 selections; Claude with socket or without wake proxy -> direct."
  focused_suites: "evidence/focused-tests.txt: 13 files (launch_data_path, codex_runtime, channel_pending_injection, codex_desktop_injection, runtime_session_restart, unattended_restart, codex_app_server_session, cielairouter_gateway_overlay, provider_gateway_options, claude_native_provider, architecture_contracts, architecture_budget, provider_contract_matrix): Ran 737 tests OK (skipped=54). Broad suites not run (instruction)."
  static: "ruff check on launch_data_path.py, runtime_launch.py, tests/test_launch_data_path.py and the evidence scripts: All checks passed. git diff --check clean on the tracked files changed here. ciel_runtime.py not touched."
  real_cli_e2e_direct: >
    evidence/e2e_plain_codex.py (real codex-tui 0.163.0 started by ciel_runtime.py --ca-runtime codex in a wt.exe console,
    isolated config G:/ciel-e2e/direct-plain/codex, loopback stub central + gateways A/B, gateway_data_path=direct).
    Facts in evidence/e2e-plain-codex/result.json, router-excerpt.txt, screen-main-*.txt, shots/01-04.png.
    Launch: launch-data-path.json codex = configured direct, active router, reason = CHANNEL_MARKER_REASON; router.log one
    WARN 'launch_data_path runtime=codex ... active=router ... elapsed_ms=0'; codex command line
    model_providers.ciel-runtime.base_url = http://127.0.0.1:<router>/v1, env_key CIEL_RUNTIME_CODEX_API_KEY,
    -m ciel-runtime-cielairouter-stub-model; only /v1/models reached the central before turn 1 (no launch-time discovery).
    Turn 1: Codex composer shows '[ciel-wake] pending_ids=1' (screen-main-01); router.log channel_stdin_proxy_injected
    transport=router display_body=False, channel_llm_wake_prompt_stripped, channel_llm_injected message_ids=1; gateway B
    request last user text 'E2E-TURN-1 please reply', no wake marker; reply STUB-REPLY-B shown (screen-main-02).
    Restart (restart_session via router /ca/mcp): codex_session_restart resumed=true claim=transport; the relaunched codex
    command line again names the router provider block; the record is unchanged (router); the restart notice turn reached
    gateway B through the router.
  restart_turn2_finding: >
    After the restart, the next channel message did not reach a gateway in either run: the restart notice (id 2, tty
    transport) was answered but its receipt failed (channel_input_receipt transcript_missing
    confirmation=awaiting_new_transcript -> channel_input_submit_unconfirmed -> prompt_not_submitted), so the router
    deferred the body of wake id 3 behind it (channel_llm_inject_deferred message_id=2 reason=input_transport_tty) and
    answered HTTP 500; Codex showed 'We're currently experiencing high demand'. The same sequence occurred in the control run
    with gateway_data_path unset (evidence/e2e-plain-codex-router/router-excerpt.txt lines for 16:57:24-16:58:02), so it is
    independent of the data-path setting and of this guard. A HEAD baseline (git archive HEAD 05a43fd, router default,
    evidence/e2e-plain-codex-router-head) could not compare it: there the console window and router were gone about 20 s
    after the restart (router.log ends at channel_windows_console_proxy_started). Cause not investigated; not fixed here.
  live_router: "127.0.0.1:9512 pid 31392 v0.2.51 /health ok before and after (evidence/live-router-before.txt, live-router-after.txt). No leftover E2E processes."
not_verified:
  - "Real Claude Code launch with session-socket input off (unit tests only)."
  - "Real codex-remote / app-server direct launch after this change (unit tests only; their direct path is unchanged apart from the explicit app_server channel declaration)."
  - "Non-Windows hosts (no such host here): plain Codex falls back there by design; the visible-body wake was not exercised."
  - "Claude Code direct with the socket temporarily unavailable types the full body through the TTY (unchanged behavior of the CIEL_RUNTIME_DIRECT_GATEWAY_ACTIVE flag); whether Windows Claude Code drops characters of a long typed body is unknown (dropping was observed for Codex on 2026-10-03)."
limits:
  - "The guard is decided at launch from the launcher's declaration; a Claude Code messaging socket that later becomes unusable does not move the running CLI back to the router."
